From 64df4d9e0c37702debc94dc7029be716add6cfdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:59:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): credit an edge-break record only within its op's
 stated width

The program sim forgave convicted columns down to a cached edge-break
record's depth, and a project file's record could state any depth - a
hand edit could hide a real gouge under an inflated bevel. Each op's
records are now held to the break width its own params state
(Chamfer2D / Deburr `width`); a wider record, or one on a kind that
declares no break, is dropped with a logged warning and its columns are
judged against the sharp model.

Pinned by edge_break_bound::{an_inflated_record_no_longer_forgives_a_deeper_cut,
an_unedited_file_still_credits_its_own_break, the_bound_reads_the_ops_own_width}.

Fixes #529

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
